  "id": "Compound::DB00758 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Clopidogrel is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through a series of interconnected molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Clopidogrel binds to Cyp2b6 and Cyp3a4, which are both involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid and quinone compounds, respectively. These interactions are linked to Cyp2c8, indicating a potential role in the metabolic activation of these substrates. The presence of a common ancestor, Thienopyridine Antiplatelet Agents, further suggests a shared regulatory mechanism involving the enzyme Cyp2c8. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency of Cyp2c8 on the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid and quinone compounds, which are influenced by Clopidogrel's pharmacological actions. The evidence supports a mechanism where Clopidogrel indirectly affects Cyp2c8 through its influence on the metabolic pathways of arachidonic acid and quinone compounds, thereby contributing to the regulation of platelet aggregation.",
